<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02T9">Remark <span data-tag="02T9">7.4.4.8</span>.</a> In the situation of Theorem <a data-tag="02T8" href="/tag/02T8">7.4.4.6</a>, the restriction map $\operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleleft } }^{\operatorname{CCart}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleleft }, \overline{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}^{\operatorname{CCart}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}})$ is automatically an isofibration of $\infty $-categories (Remark <a data-tag="02T5" href="/tag/02T5">5.3.1.18</a>). Using Proposition <a data-tag="01G7" href="/tag/01G7">4.5.6.20</a>, we see that condition $(1)$ of Theorem <a data-tag="02T8" href="/tag/02T8">7.4.4.6</a> is equivalent to the following <em>a priori</em> stronger condition: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1')$</dt>
<dd><p>
The restriction map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleleft } }^{\operatorname{CCart}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleleft }, \overline{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}^{\operatorname{CCart}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \]
</div>
<p>
 is a trivial Kan fibration of simplicial sets. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
